# Single source of truth for the PostgreSQL/PostGIS image this project targets.
#
# Production reports PostgreSQL major version 17 (confirmed by commit fcd50b5,
# "match restore-drill Postgres image to production's major version" --
# ci/docker-compose.database-recovery.yml). Every environment that tests
# against a Postgres container -- CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml), the
# Production Deployment Gate (.github/workflows/production-gate.yml,
# ci/docker-compose.production-gate.yml), and the performance baseline
# (performance/docker-compose.performance.yml) -- must use the exact same
# image so a PostGIS 3.4-vs-3.5 or Postgres 16-vs-17 behavior difference is
# never caught for the first time in production.
#
# scripts/database/check-postgres-version-consistency.sh reads this file and
# fails CI if any workflow or compose file under .github/workflows/, ci/, or
# performance/ references a different postgis/postgis tag. Update this file
# first when the target version changes, then re-run that script locally
# before touching any other file -- it will name every place still needing
# the update.
POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgis/postgis:17-3.5
